+    // Never copy past the destination subresource. The footprint is sized as
+    // the guest mip reduced then scaled while the host mip is the base scaled
+    // then reduced, so the deepest mips of scaled textures can be a row or
+    // column larger (Xenia clamps this too); clamp against the actual
